{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at exact clean head ac2dd80fbff0cc3351d4348adbe3398ab701bfbe (branch request/needs-action-ratification).\n\nThe board itself: the ratification population, its count line, its disclosure, and the tests that pin them.\n\nSelf-initiated work carrying forward the substance of retired request 4c739023, on hugh's authorization of 2026-08-22. This is the repair head for codex's changes-requested 28720650 on 94f2d8f5, which I ratified.\n\nWhat the change does: workRows iterates projection.commitments, and ratification is not a commitment, so the one duty only a ratifier can discharge was the population the board could not display. It is now a third population beside the two summary lines already there, each reached from its own count and never summed into one figure with them. Which kinds are owed is read from the vocabulary - satisfier role:ratifier and a render that is not note - so a kind declared later is classified by its own definition. Measured against this log the queue is 15: propose=14, roster=1. Reading the vocabulary also admits admission-profile, infra-key, kind-def and seal, none of which a hand-written list would have carried.\n\nWhat this head fixes over 94f2d8f5. The committed internal/service/uidist bundle now matches the reviewed source: I had changed UI source without running make ui-check, so gs serve would have shipped the old build. And the unresolved-ratifier disclosure is now pinned by a DOM test that opens the population with zero, two and one ratifier and asserts the warning present when it should be and absent when it should not. Codex found that setting the condition to false left all 68 tests green - every assertion about it was a doesNotMatch on the resolved case, which any missing element satisfies. Mutating it to false now fails.\n\nGates at this exact head: npx tsc --noEmit clean, npm test 69 pass 0 fail, make ui-check clean. No Go source changed beyond the regenerated embed.","body":{"commit":"ac2dd80fbff0cc33